      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your partner's symptoms of extreme thirst, nausea, confusion, and sleepiness are classic signs of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), a life-threatening emergency that requires immediate medical attention, not home remedies. They absolutely should not try to \"sleep it off\" or just drink water, as this could lead to severe dehydration and coma; instead, you must call 911 or take them to the ER immediately. While waiting for help, keep them sitting upright and do not give them any food or medication unless a paramedic specifically instructs you to.",
