      "content": "Giving them a full dose of insulin now is a catastrophic mistake that will crash their blood sugar instantly, causing severe hypoglycemia, seizures, and potentially death before the ambulance even arrives.\nYou must administer only a tiny fraction of their usual dose if you have a glucometer, but honestly, you should just call 911 immediately because driving them yourself in this state is incredibly dangerous and could kill them on the road.\nDo not try to \"fix it yourself\" with home remedies or partial doses; the confusion and nausea indicate their body is already failing, and only a hospital can reverse this specific type of diabetic emergency safely.\nPlease call 911 right this second, or if you absolutely cannot, drive them to the ER immediately rather than waiting for an ambulance that might take too long.",
